# Phrases that may stay as plain text, one per line, matched without regard
# to case.  Keep this list short.  Each phrase is the text of a message that
# a program writes, or a name that only looks like a path, a command or a
# variable.  A phrase protects the 40 characters around it.
#
# The fields of the Pathname and Filename markers: PATH, FNAME and the other
# words are the text that the marker prints, not the variable of the system.
Pathname | Long | PATH
Pathname | PATH |
DATE, TIME, FNAME, PATH, PRINTER, REV
Name: [PATH]
# Messages with a place holder in the text of a message of a program.
Settings saved to PATH
Cannot run the editor: PATH
was not found in PATH
or in PATH.
Print needs LaTeX: pdflatex
Wrote FILE.pdf
# The prefix key of a terminal multiplexer is a key, not a directory.
a prefix key
the prefix of the multiplexer
Terminal: key prefix
